(: The direct teaching of the Hara across traditions (

    Always consider this view and perspective: This direct teaching is the highest and most secret teaching in all enlightenment and Bodhisattva traditions. This is because it is pointing directly at a direct experience, unique to each individual but with common method. Luang Por Wat Pak Nam said that this gate is the same gate all Buddhas pass through. Zen enlightenment kensho by focusing on hara and bringing mind there and doing everything from it (Samurai, Miyamoto Musashi). Chinese zen unborn mind (Bankei, Huang Po) (The unborn mind at the origin of thought when settled into is total liberation and there is no other, all thought originates from the Hara, realizing the unborn is entering union with the Hara). Dhammakaya Thai Buddhism (Focusing on the stillness at the gravitational center of the body, which is the hara two inches above the center of the belly button, and is also a light center, and you repeatedly stop at that center, and mind originates from it). New age and Channelled materials e.g. Law of One Ra, Amenti channels, Thoth etc. (The solar plexus or yellow ray governs the body, is the center of the will which is the lifd force). Satipanya Mahasi Sayadaw Vispassana Buddhist Meditation e.g. Daniel Ingram MCTB (Attaining awareness of pure body sensation is pure awareness without moving mind from the body, which is attained by resting at the hara). This is full enlightenment and total freedom from karma as it is the relinquishment of will into God. Without movement of the mind desire does not form as arisen thought. Shamanic Indigenous and Modern Gaian Lineages (Synesthesia of senses, single sense door, is natural mind and shamanic thought that directly visions space and time and can journey, can be cultivated by dissolving the stranglehold of thought interfering with the senses, merging and expanding a sense until it becomes anothee, which is the same natural, gentle thought that is the unmitigated enlightened mind at the bright center of the still Hara). Advaita Vedanta, Indian Enlightenment Schools e.g. Ramana Maharshi, Anandamayi Ma, J. Krish, U.G Krish (Total union with Brahman 'God' as 'Self' which is Yoga, union of mind with body, which is the state where mind is unmoved in nondual stillness). Christian Enlightenment Mystics e.g. Bernadette Roberts (God is stillness at the center of the body and consciousness is the reflecting mirror of the self on the self, resolved when you are taken into the absolute emptiness and stillness at the center). Vajrayana, Dzogchen and Bon e.g. Chogyam trungpa, Dilgo Khyentse (Natural mind is vivid and empty, which is the natural enlightened perception, and all obscurations can cease through sudden dissolution of all kinds of tension. The mind outside of the Hara, stillness without thought is attunement to Buddha-mind, and it dissolves tensions. I know this as I have realized it myself through a combination of contemplating all these methods. My mind is permanently settled into the hara.

) End The direct teaching of the Hara across traditions :) With gratitude for this reading
